@startuml correction-dimensions
' The N heterogeneous "dimensions" of approximate matching, each with its own
' metric/engine, unified into one joint score by a semiring. Colour groups a
' dimension with the crate that provides it.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-dimensions.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/integration/lling-llang/hierarchical-correction.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title <latex>N</latex>-dimensional approximate matching — heterogeneous axes fused by a semiring

rectangle "**noisy channel**\n<latex>\hat{w} = \operatorname*{argmax}\, \mathbb{P}(x \mid w) \cdot \mathbb{P}(w)</latex>" as nc #455A64

rectangle "**DIM 1 · Orthographic**\nedit distance (a metric)\nliblevenshtein automaton" as d1 #1565C0
rectangle "**DIM 2 · Phonetic**\narticulatory sound-alike\nliblevenshtein — fused with DIM 1 in <latex>T_{\text{lex}}</latex>" as d2 #1E88E5
rectangle "**DIM 3 · Syntactic**\nCFG membership (constraint)\nlling-llang CfgFilter" as d3 #6A1B9A
rectangle "**DIM 4 · Contextual**\n<latex>-\log \mathbb{P}(w \mid \text{ctx})</latex> (likelihood)\nlibgrammstein MKN n-gram" as d4 #2E7D32
rectangle "**DIM 5 · Semantic**\ncos-similarity → pseudo-<latex>\mathbb{P}</latex>\nlibgrammstein embeddings" as d5 #388E3C

rectangle "**Semiring**  <latex>(K, \oplus, \otimes, \bar{0}, \bar{1})</latex>\n<latex>\otimes</latex> combines factors along a path\n<latex>\oplus</latex> selects among competing paths\nTropical: <latex>(\min, +)</latex>   Log: <latex>(\operatorname{logsumexp}, +)</latex>" as sr #00838F
rectangle "**joint score**\nbest correction = shortest / max-<latex>\mathbb{P}</latex> path" as js #455A64

nc --> d1 : channel
nc --> d2 : channel
nc --> d3 : prior
nc --> d4 : prior
nc --> d5 : prior

d1 --> sr
d2 --> sr
d3 --> sr
d4 --> sr
d5 --> sr
sr --> js

note bottom of sr
  The dimensions are **heterogeneous** —
  metric / likelihood / constraint. The
  semiring is the common currency that
  makes them composable. Each independent
  factor is one dimension → the WFST product
  construction makes the joint search N-D.
end note
@enduml
